From 3940c1410c48cd832124f1e2620905333442c1a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:32:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 082/106] wifi: xradio: Drop the vif lock when a TX confirm
 finds no queued packet

xrwl_hwpriv_to_vifpriv() returns with priv->vif_lock held, and every path
of xradio_tx_confirm_cb() must release it. When xradio_queue_get_skb()
fails, neither the requeue branch nor the success branch runs, and the
function returns with the lock held. That happens when the firmware
confirms a frame that a deauth already flushed (the WARN at
xradio_queue_get_skb). The next wsm_get_tx() in the bh thread then spins on
the lock forever. The resulting RCU stall wedges deauth
(synchronize_rcu_expedited), rtnl users (iw, ip) and even mount.

Seen on the TrimUI Smart Pro when switching from a WPA3 network back to
WPA2 during traffic. Two connect/disconnect rounds with a ping flood
during the disconnect now pass without a hang. The late-confirm path did
not trigger in those rounds, so the fix is verified by code inspection.

Such a late confirm is a normal path, so it no longer WARNs (neither
here nor in xradio_queue_get_skb() on a generation mismatch); it is
logged with a rate-limited debug message.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/xradio/queue.c |  2 +-
 drivers/net/wireless/xradio/tx.c    | 14 ++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/queue.c b/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/queue.c
index 53b72f804..51420f089 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/queue.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/queue.c
@@ -671,7 +671,7 @@ int xradio_queue_get_skb(struct xradio_queue *queue, u32 packetID,
 		WARN_ON(1);
 		ret = -EINVAL;
 	} else if (unlikely(item->generation != item_generation)) {
-		WARN_ON(1);
+		/* Already flushed (e.g. on deauth): a late TX confirm. */
 		ret = -ENOENT;
 	} else {
 		*skb = item->skb;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/tx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/tx.c
index 4ad5e1118..60478bf73 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/xradio/tx.c
@@ -1153,8 +1153,7 @@ void xradio_tx_confirm_cb(struct xradio_common *hw_priv,
 		}
 		spin_unlock_bh(&priv->ps_state_lock);
 		spin_unlock(&priv->vif_lock);
-	} else if (!WARN_ON(xradio_queue_get_skb(
-			queue, arg->packetID, &skb, &txpriv))) {
+	} else if (!xradio_queue_get_skb(queue, arg->packetID, &skb, &txpriv)) {
 		struct ieee80211_tx_info *tx = IEEE80211_SKB_CB(skb);
 		struct ieee80211_hdr *frame = (struct ieee80211_hdr *)&skb->data[txpriv->offset];
 		int tx_count = arg->ackFailures;
@@ -1286,6 +1285,17 @@ void xradio_tx_confirm_cb(struct xradio_common *hw_priv,
 
 
 		xradio_queue_remove(queue, arg->packetID);
+	} else {
+		/*
+		 * The packet is gone from the queue (flushed on deauth, for
+		 * example) and the firmware confirmed it late. The vif lock
+		 * taken by xrwl_hwpriv_to_vifpriv() must still be dropped,
+		 * otherwise the next wsm_get_tx() spins on it forever.
+		 */
+		dev_dbg_ratelimited(hw_priv->pdev,
+				    "TX confirm for flushed packet 0x%08x\n",
+				    arg->packetID);
+		spin_unlock(&priv->vif_lock);
 	}
 }
 
